'''''Lysimachia minima''''' ('''chaffweed''') is a 1-4&nbsp;inch (2–10&nbsp;cm) [[perennial]] [[herbaceous plant|herb]] in the primula family ([[Primulaceae]]).  A cosmopolitan species, this small plant is native widely across North America and Eurasia.<ref>[http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=242416059 Flora of North America]</ref> It can be found growing in moist soils and [[vernal pool|seasonal pools]].<ref name= burke/><ref name= grin>{{GRIN | accessdate=2010-03-27 }}</ref>

